    "notes": "The 2026-4 guide confirms the 18 November 2026, 5pm deadline and 9 March 2027 decision date; its footers retain 2026-3. The main page now lists 2027 rounds. The guide permits a £250,000 maximum project cost, while the eligibility checker says less than £250,000. Applicants must own, lease or formally manage the site. The checker also requires project completion and funding claims within 12 months of a funding decision. A CTP payment of 10.75% of the grant is compulsory, payable directly to FCC Environment within 28 days of request. The funder expressly excludes this from project costs and distinguishes it from match funding; no universal project match contribution is specified. Funding gaps must have pending applications or identified prospects. The document list is selective: the guide also requests authorisation minutes, site photos and maps, works drawings, relevant access policies, consents, evidence of need and support, cost breakdowns and cost evidence, and confirmed match-funding evidence. Renewable-energy projects require an EPC or PEA. Required uploads may follow within five days. Initial cost evidence may be a supplier quote, architect/QS estimate or comparable-project costs; full competitive quotes follow success. Further information, ENTRUST registration and a signed Funding Agreement follow approval.",
